{"title":"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Hint\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Hint</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Using_Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Using Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91381b367f9753ded66ab981c7451f2cb117578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OABC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> are extended past <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to meet the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. What is the area of the shaded region in the figure, which is bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and the minor arc connecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c262c3de70ae89ba3efff503f9573d3a8b5f46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); pair O=origin, A=(1,0), C=(0,1), B=(1,1), D=(1, sqrt(3)), E=(sqrt(3), 1), point=B; fill(Arc(O, 2, 0, 90)--O--cycle, mediumgray); clip(B--Arc(O, 2, 30, 60)--cycle); draw(Circle(origin, 2)); draw((-2,0)--(2,0)^^(0,-2)--(0,2)); draw(A--D^^C--E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(point--A)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(point--C)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, dir(point--O)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(point--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(point--E)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/493894bcebc41ba1a95ccb5a24528b5c519e9460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{3}+1-\\sqrt{3}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{2}(2-\\sqrt{3}) \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\pi(2-\\sqrt{3})\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{2}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{3}-1+\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"745\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Hint\">Hint</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Hint\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Indeed, this is the trap answer, coming from believing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd086bfde3cbcd3899095243a222eee23e40b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> is a quarter circle. An easy way to see this is that, if it really were a quarter circle, its circumference curves more \"inward\" rather than on the circumference of the circle. Be careful!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The shaded area is equivalent to the area of sector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> minus the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> plus the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd086bfde3cbcd3899095243a222eee23e40b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/237ae3619645e900fe99f9d535c417dcdcf28d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(DA)^2=(CE)^2=2^2-1^2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"19\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e6af671ba8694bf09b71cb0ef8cc03eb9886364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=CE=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1449f9c78df10e5e3afe22131e754813b5bdf856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOA$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33dc6f29fb980fcdf0551a878a8bfb7f7a4de74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EOC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c95ac412f6963c7df84ea44a9ee0ad954d0769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EOC = \\angle DOA = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"185\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91381b367f9753ded66ab981c7451f2cb117578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OABC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is a square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e7dbea252ee8764607eec6d303c31fffab4f149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COA = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1c372a7653084bd8f4913d852a9f56bba50f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DOE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> can be found by doing some subtraction of angles. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735d59bc76c8b253255341f4032a3eff047019d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COA - \\angle DOA = \\angle DOC = \\angle EOA$\" width=\"294\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a21723f4abba6ee2b4271edcc0964e3a7a768df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ - 60^\\circ = \\angle EOA = 30^\\circ$\" width=\"201\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/7472f53a8d674c681a9e8dc112a46a24f1989ced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DOA - \\angle EOA = \\angle DOE$\" width=\"215\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e59a846f6452a5ccd46f5d987f2f9afb70fbced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ - 30^\\circ = \\angle DOE = 30^\\circ$\" width=\"203\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>So, the area of sector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9282e78facf7fe97dc487a4c1caaa65e0d9851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{360} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 2^2 = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d67bc2a188e9626406b74ee5308da27c68890ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\sin 30^\\circ = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"154\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a5482e2df77a27420825081bb54e937069afc406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=CB=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caf3439e55c1afbdf15c96fccf39c731bb726381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB=EB=(\\sqrt{3}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"21\" />. So, the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd086bfde3cbcd3899095243a222eee23e40b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af6f7ded5326ee34e85010e5bfb3cd416f1cafaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (\\sqrt{3}-1)^2 = 2-\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"185\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the shaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5286dd5473d045933993507794a26edcdc263b89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{\\pi}{3}) - (1) + (2-\\sqrt{3}) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{3} + 1 - \\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"332\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>OR\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34db479782fad4b5b377a6840ac23bfcfef4e871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ODA}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> has the same height as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1650795e456a6fb48c9aad446b1239df04d0f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{OBD}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We already know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891b266697238fa7df21b7cbb1b9453f5b4ce1c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = \\sqrt{3} - 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Therefore the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1650795e456a6fb48c9aad446b1239df04d0f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{OBD}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/d/20db91f337449a2d0337cb2e834e5072a2880acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{3}-1) \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"205\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/e/5de746609b4d2207294f4d12055ede3d2e54e546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{OBD} = \\triangle{OBE} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"232\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Therefore the sum of the areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca44df0074de8880e51a8e759c2a4e61f11b1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2} = \\sqrt{3}-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"165\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Then the area of the shaded area becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88a6dbb2c1537e35a482d40da0c78638efe2bd80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3} - (\\sqrt{3} - 1) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{3} +1 - \\sqrt{3}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"278\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the Pythagorean Theorem, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c124b320353f3c26c8bf067b62cd3e6952b22798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB = DA - BA = \\sqrt{3} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"213\" height=\"18\" />. The area of the shaded element is the area of sector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> minus the areas of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0abc16524278d75c49c3981a83ecc8f2f05440ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBO$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f615fbbc178c1150def431902f9f0762e2f13537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBO$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> combined. Below is an image to help.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d58d52353c6b457465beaae9cf5af0d5170f0dab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); pair O=origin, A=(1,0), C=(0,1), B=(1,1), D=(1, sqrt(3)), E=(sqrt(3), 1), point=B; fill(Arc(O, 2, 0, 90)--O--cycle, mediumgray); clip(B--Arc(O, 2, 30, 60)--cycle); draw(Circle(origin, 2)); draw((-2,0)--(2,0)^^(0,-2)--(0,2)); draw(A--D^^C--E^^D--O^^E--O^^B--O); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(point--A)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(point--C)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, dir(point--O)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(point--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(point--E)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (1.33,1.04), SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n</p><p>Using the Base Altitude formula, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are the bases and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> are the altitudes, respectively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/c/2fcaaf1bb48afb8d4e432eb7f6f3eda97a249a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DBO] = [EBO] = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"215\" height=\"41\" />. The area of sector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10f7b229549d9afbdef6ae2862bc89bacfe16cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The area of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72a1caa0cb9e0f72f414ebd8180ea676808568f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, and therefore we have the area of sector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd086bfde3cbcd3899095243a222eee23e40b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e818736eb5ddf25a8db41caf007d84f01694a19a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{3} + 1 - \\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"142\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Using_Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Using_Answer_Choices)\">Solution 3 (Using Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Using Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like the first solutions, you find that the area of sector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d0dc818ffa40c824ec87c9ad9c51fa86f458d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />. We also know that the triangles will not be in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/186d9d976137aae10566722f246f64338c4bba0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\pi}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. Looking at the answers, choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5bdc2c0e59651ee5e6fa74ba318dc73d744feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb3626ff02d0ba34a6ae1421f4b5e155992ec4cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> both contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d0dc818ffa40c824ec87c9ad9c51fa86f458d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />. However, based on the diagram, we observe that the answer must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db45d4c7bbac0bf556adc6c55cd68c524f578f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />. Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e818736eb5ddf25a8db41caf007d84f01694a19a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{3} + 1 - \\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"142\" height=\"46\" /> consists of a value less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d0dc818ffa40c824ec87c9ad9c51fa86f458d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We calculate the shaded area by subtracting the unshaded area in the quarter circle from a quarter circle, which consists of two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/2258a8895f62bd87b4ae22829a3ab7515de9b169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 ^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> sectors and two 30-60-90 triangles minus a square. The area of the shaded region is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28dea2ba67e2859ff3393d6258be509beb6d85ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\pi \\times 2^2}{4} - 2 ( \\frac {\\pi \\times 2^2}{12} + \\frac {\\sqrt 3}{2} - 1 ) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{3} + 1 - \\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"401\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~thatmathsguy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BmIXToyrZzY?list=PLoZ0gn0j87fcm-YyWXXnIdAcT5NLq9W2i&amp;t=1801\">https://youtu.be/BmIXToyrZzY?list=PLoZ0gn0j87fcm-YyWXXnIdAcT5NLq9W2i&amp;t=1801</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"m